---**Example**
---
---```cpp
---dm::LinalgMatrix A({1, 1, 1}, 3, 1), b({1, 2, 3}, 3, 1);
---std::print("{:.0f}\n", A.solve(b).values()[0]); // 2
---```
---
---**Errors** (raised as Lua errors)
---* `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible/wide shapes or nonfinite solve inputs.
---* `std::runtime_error`: For singular or rank-deficient systems.
---@param rhs datamunge.LinalgMatrix Matrix of right-hand sides with rows() rows.
---@return datamunge.LinalgMatrix # Owned dense solution snapshot.
function datamunge.LinalgMatrix:solve(rhs) end

---Evaluate once into an owned snapshot with no deferred operands.
