---@param function_ datamunge.ArbitraryFunction Objective to minimise.
---@param lower number[] Lower corner of the box.
---@param upper number[] Upper corner of the box (each entry larger than in `lower`).
---@param surrogate datamunge.BayesianSurrogate Surrogate refitted before every proposal.
---@return datamunge.BayesianOptimizationResult # The evaluations and the best point.
function datamunge.BayesianOptimization:run(function_, lower, upper, surrogate) end

---Runs the loop and returns only the best value.
---
---**Errors** (raised as Lua errors)
---* `std::invalid_argument`: If the bounds do not match `coordinates` or are not increasing.
---@param function_ datamunge.ArbitraryFunction Objective to minimise.
---@param coordinates number[] Output: the best point (its length must equal the bounds').
---@param lower number[] Lower corner of the box.
---@param upper number[] Upper corner of the box.
---@param surrogate datamunge.BayesianSurrogate Surrogate refitted before every proposal.
---@return number # The smallest observed value.
function datamunge.BayesianOptimization:optimize(function_, coordinates, lower, upper, surrogate) end

