---Model orders and optimizer settings for an ARIMA fit.
---
---The regular orders are (p, d, q) and the seasonal orders are (P, D, Q) with period s.
---Leave every seasonal field at zero for a plain ARIMA(p, d, q) model.
---@class datamunge.ARIMAOptions
---@field p integer Non-seasonal AR order (p).
---@field d integer Non-seasonal differencing order (d).
---@field q integer Non-seasonal MA order (q).
---@field seasonal_p integer Seasonal AR order (P).
---@field seasonal_d integer Seasonal differencing order (D).
---@field seasonal_q integer Seasonal MA order (Q).
---@field seasonal_period integer Seasonal period (s); must be nonzero when P, D, or Q is nonzero.
---@field include_mean boolean Fit an intercept (mean of the fully-differenced series). Only meaningful when d == 0 && seasonal_d == 0 -- matching R's arima(), a mean term is not fit on a series that has already been differenced to stationarity.
---@field de_population_size integer Population size of the differential-evolution optimizer.
---@field de_max_generations integer Maximum number of differential-evolution generations.
---@field coefficient_bound number Box constraint [-bound, bound] applied to every AR/MA coefficient during optimization.
---@field seed integer Random seed for the differential-evolution optimizer.
---@overload fun(): datamunge.ARIMAOptions
datamunge.ARIMAOptions = {}

---A Box-Jenkins seasonal ARIMA(p, d, q)(P, D, Q)_s model, fit to a single numeric
---series by conditional sum of squares (CSS): the series is differenced (regular
---d times, then seasonal D times with period s) to stationarity, the combined
---AR/MA polynomials (regular composed with seasonal, via polynomial multiplication)
---are estimated by minimizing the conditional residual sum of squares with
---DifferentialEvolution, and forecasts are produced by recursing the fitted
---difference equation forward and re-integrating through the differencing steps.
---
---Setting seasonal_period == 0 (the default) reduces this to a plain, non-seasonal
---ARIMA(p, d, q) model -- i.e. SARIMA is the general case, ARIMA the special case,
---exactly as in R's arima()/statsmodels' SARIMAX().
---
---Note: CSS estimation approximates the exact Gaussian likelihood by conditioning
---on the first max(p + P*s, q + Q*s) observations rather than filtering the full
---series (e.g. via a Kalman filter); it is a standard, textbook ARIMA fitting
---method (R's arima(method = "CSS")) but will differ slightly from exact-ML fits.
---@class datamunge.ARIMA
---@overload fun(y: number[], options?: datamunge.ARIMAOptions): datamunge.ARIMA
datamunge.ARIMA = {}

---The options the model was fit with.
---@return datamunge.ARIMAOptions # The stored ARIMAOptions.
function datamunge.ARIMA:options() end

---Fitted non-seasonal AR coefficients
---
---`\phi_1,\dots,\phi_p`.
---
---`1-\sum_i\phi_i B^i`.
---@return number[] # A vector of length p; the AR polynomial is
function datamunge.ARIMA:ar_coefficients() end

---Fitted non-seasonal MA coefficients
---
---`\theta_1,\dots,\theta_q`.
---
---`1+\sum_j\theta_j B^j`.
---@return number[] # A vector of length q; the MA polynomial is
function datamunge.ARIMA:ma_coefficients() end

---Fitted seasonal AR coefficients
---
---`\Phi_1,\dots,\Phi_P`.
---
---`1-\sum_i\Phi_i B^{is}`.
---@return number[] # A vector of length P; the polynomial is
function datamunge.ARIMA:seasonal_ar_coefficients() end

---Fitted seasonal MA coefficients
---
---`\Theta_1,\dots,\Theta_Q`.
---
---`1+\sum_j\Theta_j B^{js}`.
---@return number[] # A vector of length Q; the polynomial is
function datamunge.ARIMA:seasonal_ma_coefficients() end

---Fitted mean of the differenced series.
---@return number # The mean, or 0 when no mean term was fit (include_mean is false, or d or D is nonzero).
function datamunge.ARIMA:mean() end

---Length of the input series.
---@return integer # The number of observations passed to the constructor.
function datamunge.ARIMA:observations() end

---Number of residuals that enter the sum of squares.
---
---`p+sP` (the conditioned-on presample).
---@return integer # The differenced series length minus
function datamunge.ARIMA:n_used() end

---Innovation variance estimate.
---@return number # The CSS residual sum of squares divided by n_used().
function datamunge.ARIMA:sigma2() end

---Gaussian log-likelihood at the CSS estimate, over n_used() residuals.
---
---`-\tfrac{n}{2}(\log 2\pi + \log\sigma^2 + 1)` with `n` = n_used().
---@return number
function datamunge.ARIMA:log_likelihood() end

---Akaike information criterion.
---
---`-2\ell + 2k`, where `k` counts the coefficients, the mean (if fit) and `\sigma^2`.
---@return number
function datamunge.ARIMA:aic() end

---Bayesian information criterion.
---
---`-2\ell + k\log n`, with `k` as in aic() and `n` = n_used().
---@return number
function datamunge.ARIMA:bic() end

---One-step-ahead fitted values on the original scale, aligned to the input
---series (the first `observations() - n_used()` entries -- the presample points
---conditioned on by CSS -- are copies of the observed value, matching a
---residual of exactly zero there rather than an undefined value).
---@return number[]
