---SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::Tape -- a reverse-mode
---("backpropagation") computation tape. Create leaf Vars against a Tape, build an
---expression out of named Var operations, then call backward() on the output Var
---to get the derivative of that output with respect to every node on the tape
---(index a leaf's own index() into the result to read its gradient).
---@class datamunge.Tape
---@overload fun(): datamunge.Tape
datamunge.Tape = {}

---Number of recorded nodes (leaves plus operation results).
---@return integer
function datamunge.Tape:size() end

---The value recorded at node `index`.
---
---**Errors** (raised as Lua errors)
---* `std::out_of_range`: When `index` >= size().
---@param index integer Node index, as returned by Var::index().
---@return number # The node's value.
function datamunge.Tape:value_at(index) end

---Reverse sweep from `output`: d(output)/d(node) for every node on the tape.
---
---The tape is unchanged, so backward() may be called again for other outputs.
---
---**Example**
---
---```cpp
---dm::Tape tape;
---const dm::Var a(tape, 2.0), b(tape, 3.0);
---const auto grad = tape.backward(a.multiply(b));
---std::print("{} {}\n", grad[a.index()], grad[b.index()]);  // 3 2
---```
---
---**Errors** (raised as Lua errors)
---* `std::out_of_range`: When `output` is not a node of this tape.
---@param output datamunge.Var A Var recorded on this tape (usually the final expression).
---@return number[] # One adjoint per node, indexed by Var::index() (0-based; add 1 in R and Lua).
