---Least-squares fits a new patch on `cell` so the whole hierarchy matches
---`values` at `points`.
---
---The patch explains only what is left after every other patch on the path (the
---residual values - evaluate(points)), in the spirit of Forsey-Bartels editing, so pass
---raw data values rather than residuals. Points are global coordinates inside the cell.
---
---**Example**
---
---```cpp
---dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
---auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
---h.fit_cell(h.root(), {b}, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {1.0, 3.0});
---std::print("{}\n", h.evaluate({0.5})); // 2
---```
---
---**Errors** (raised as Lua errors)
---* `std::out_of_range`: For an invalid id.
---* `std::invalid_argument`: If the cell has a patch, inputs are empty/mismatched, or a point lies outside the cell.
---* `std::runtime_error`: If the local normal equations are singular.
---@param cell integer Cell id; must not already have a patch (clear_spline() first to refit).
---@param bases datamunge.BSplineBasis[] Patch bases on [0, 1], one per dimension.
---@param points number[][] Sample locations inside the cell.
---@param values number[] One raw data value per point.
---@param options? datamunge.SplineSolveOptions Solver settings. (default: `datamunge.SplineSolveOptions()`)
function datamunge.HierarchicalBSpline:fit_cell(cell, bases, points, values, options) end

